1. PRODUCT VISION
=======================================================================

PRODUCT NAME: Chakki

Chakki is a developer-focused AI engineering platform.

It is built around ONE canonical execution engine and multiple clients.

TARGET PRODUCT FAMILY:

1. Chakki Engine
   Headless task runtime, conversation state, persistent history, model
   gateway, tool execution, approvals, verification, agent orchestration.

2. Chakki CLI / TUI
   First-class terminal interface. Not a debug-only side project.

3. Chakki Studio
   Professional desktop interface with live agent activity, workspace
   navigation, tool execution, reviewable diffs, sessions and task timeline.

4. Future clients
   Web/cloud execution, IDE integrations, and mobile clients. They must use
   the same engine contracts. They are not a reason to create competing
   agent runtimes now.

The current project is an implementation experiment until it passes the
defined acceptance gates. Do not automatically replace the canonical
Chakki repository or claim that this experiment is production-ready.

The product must be useful even when the user does not know which provider,
context budget, retry state, or internal worker is currently active.

The primary differentiators are:

A. Persistent, addressable, lossless conversation history.
B. Deterministic and provenance-aware memory retrieval without required
   embeddings or a local inference model.
C. Reliable tool execution with observable results.
D. Director-mode orchestration with specialized subagents.
E. A responsive, keyboard-first UI that presents real operational state.
F. Dynamic access to models offered by Kilo Gateway, including currently
   available free models.
G. A replaceable client architecture.

Do not attempt to win by copying another product's name, assets, private
implementation, or pixel-perfect design. Use established products as
behavioral and usability references. Chakki must have its own identity.

