100k event tests must be bounded, deterministic and reproducible.
Do not place a 100k-event synthetic fixture into every ordinary unit test.

=======================================================================
19. SECURITY AND RED-TEAM READINESS
=======================================================================

Security must be part of the engine, not a UI checkbox.

Threat model:
- malicious repository instructions;
- prompt injection from files, tool output, web pages, MCP tools and history;
- path traversal and symlink escapes;
- shell argument injection;
- TOCTOU file changes;
- secrets in environment/config/logs/output;
- unauthorized local clients;
- session/run/approval identifier guessing;
- concurrent client races;
- malicious skills/plugins/MCP servers;
- corrupted ledger/index;
- poisoned tool output;
- dependency/supply-chain risks;
- denial of service through excessive output/tasks/large inputs;
- network egress without permission.

Required controls:
- default-deny external tool network access;
- explicit allowlist for permitted network capabilities;
- workspace path jail checked at execution time;
- safe process launch without shell-string concatenation where avoidable;
- process groups, deadlines and output limits;
- per-session capabilities and authorization;
- token redaction;
- typed errors;
- signed/verified plugin artifacts where supported;
- explicit trust state for third-party tools;
- immutable audit events for consequential actions;
- no untrusted retrieved text promoted into system instructions;
- least-privilege subprocess environment;
- bounded concurrent agents and requests;
- security test fixtures and mutation tests.

Use real platform isolation mechanisms where available. Do not declare
sandboxing active merely because an abstract Sandbox interface exists.

Autopilot may pre-authorize reversible workspace-local actions according to
policy. It must not remove all security boundaries.

The tool must state clearly when an action was blocked by policy and how an
authorized operator can change the configured policy.

