22. GOLDEN USER JOURNEY
=======================================================================

The required product path:

1. User opens the project workspace.
2. User sees the actual engine connection status.
3. User selects a model from the live catalogue.
4. User submits a real task.
5. Engine creates a durable task/session record.
6. UI receives task.started and task.progress from the real runtime.
7. Engine requests a real provider completion.
8. Provider response is streamed and parsed.
9. If a tool is needed, the tool schema and permission policy are validated.
10. A real proposed change is persisted with a before hash and actual diff.
11. UI shows the diff and approval requirement.
12. Rejection causes no protected disk mutation.
13. Approval passes the canonical authorization boundary.
14. The worker applies the patch and records the real filesystem result.
15. Relevant tests run through the real command/test runtime.
16. Results and artifacts are recorded.
17. The independent verifier checks the result.
18. Task completion is reported only from observed state.
19. Original messages, tool outputs, events and artifacts remain addressable.
20. The user can close the app, restart the engine, reconnect and inspect
    the same session with its integrity validated.

Build a real integration test around this path.
Use a disposable, isolated test repository and deterministic provider fixtures
for offline runs. Run a separate real Kilo smoke only if network use has been
explicitly enabled.

Do not fake streaming or filesystem effects to make the golden journey pass.

