23. DEFINITION OF DONE
=======================================================================

A capability is done only when all of these exist:
- implementation in the real execution path;
- explicit error behavior;
- permission behavior;
- deterministic unit tests;
- integration coverage at the real boundary;
- user-visible truthful status;
- documentation of limits;
- reproducible test command;
- passing current-source verification.

A visually present button is not done.
A source file existing is not done.
A successful build alone is not done.
A synthetic transcript is not done.
A mocked provider is not live provider verification.
A local preview is not a signed native installer.
A test skipped because of unavailable tools is not a pass.

No fixed latency claim is accepted without measurement.
No platform-support claim is accepted without build evidence.
No security claim is accepted without a defined threat and tested boundary.

